type: software
title: "SWSANS"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-16
authors:
  - family-names: Adams
    given-names: Michael P.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9269-8087"
abstract: >-
  SWSANS is a tested Python implementation for simulating randomly oriented
  Stoner-Wohlfarth particle ensembles with uniaxial, cubic, or additive aligned
  uniaxial-cubic anisotropy. It connects Landau-Lifshitz field sweeps to
  hysteresis, magnetization correlation tensors, and unpolarized and
  polarization-averaged spin-flip magnetic small-angle neutron scattering
  observables in perpendicular and parallel scattering geometries. A
  browser-native interface performs the calculations locally.
keywords:
  - Stoner-Wohlfarth model
  - magnetic hysteresis
  - magnetic small-angle neutron scattering
  - SANS
  - Landau-Lifshitz dynamics
  - magnetic nanoparticles
  - scientific software
